N = json.loads("""{"sum":["<b>SOS is 48.3% (−2.5 pp vs last wave).</b> On the 206 stores audited in both waves it fell 1.8 pp with availability unchanged, so it is a real decline, not a sample effect. PEP still leads KO (20.7%), but “Others” rose to 25.6% (+3.8 pp): the share lost went to other products, not to KO.","<b>Availability is the root cause.</b> Only 48.8% of Petro stores have a PEP cooler, flat for six waves; 125 of 244 stores have none. PEP SOS is 61.5% where a PEP cooler exists vs 35.7% where it does not. Indicative: 70% availability would lift national SOS to about 53.7%, and 90% to about 58.9%.","<b>Fullness is healthy (93.5%, up from 90.7% six waves ago). Purity is the in-cooler problem:</b> 75.9% (−2.1 pp). Of the space in PEP coolers, 14.1% holds other products, 6.0% KO and 3.9% MBL. Utilization (Fullness × Purity) is 71.0% (−1.5 pp), so its drop is purity-driven.","<b>Weakest cities:</b> Faisalabad 24.8% (availability 13%, only city where KO is ahead of PEP), Lahore 35.5% (−6.8 pp; availability 34.5%, “Others” at 41.8%) and Karachi 48.7% (availability 40%). <b>Multan fell the most (−9.9 pp)</b> because Purity (−7.7 pp) and Fullness slipped even though availability is 89%.","<b>Strong cities:</b> Peshawar is the benchmark (95% availability, 62.6% SOS). Rawalpindi and Islamabad lead on brand share but have cooler-placement gaps. Sukkur has only 2 stores (target 10), so it cannot be judged.","<b>Competition:</b> Coke is ahead of Pepsi nationally (9.8% vs 8.1% of cooler facings), widest in Faisalabad, Lahore, Multan and Karachi. 7UP is level with Sprite (8.8% vs 8.6%) and Mirinda is ahead of Fanta (4.4% vs 3.5%). Pepsi leads Coke in Gujranwala, Peshawar, Rawalpindi and Islamabad."],"why":["SOS −2.5 pp splits into: stores without a PEP cooler −1.7 pp, stores with a PEP cooler −0.6 pp, availability mix −0.2 pp. Most of the loss is where PEP has no cooler.","“Others” rose from 21.8% to 25.6% while KO slipped from 21.7% to 20.7%. The competitor taking shelf in Petro is increasingly non-KO products in other coolers.","Where there is no PEP cooler, 79% of stores have only another brand’s cooler, 15% have a KO cooler and 6% have no cooler at all.","Inside PEP coolers: 94% of coolers are switched on, 53 of 119 are not 100% full, and 50 of 119 (42%) have purity below 70%."],"c":{"Karachi":{"tag":"Availability + purity","drag":"Availability","why":["Availability 40.0%: 30 of 50 stores have no PEP cooler. Of those, 30% have a KO cooler, 60% only another brand’s cooler and 10% no cooler.","Only 83.3% of installed PEP coolers are switched on, a quick fix.","Purity 69.4% (+2.0 pp): 25.4% of PEP-cooler facings are other products; KO is only 3.1%. Fullness is 100%, not an issue.","SOS fell 3.0 pp, mainly from stores without a PEP cooler (−4.5 pp effect). Coke 11.0% is ahead of Pepsi 9.6%; 7UP leads Sprite."]},"Sukkur":{"tag":"Low base","drag":"–","why":["Only 2 stores audited (PEP panel target is 10), both with a PEP cooler. Purity 96.2%, SOS 69.2%.","Too small to draw conclusions. Receiving the full panel is the first step."]},"Multan":{"tag":"Biggest fall","drag":"Purity / Fullness","why":["SOS 55.7%, down 9.9 pp, the largest fall. Availability is fine (89.3%), so the loss is inside the cooler.","Purity −7.7 pp to 74.8%: MBL takes 8.4%, other products 10.3% and KO 5.9% of PEP-cooler facings.","Fullness 89.6%: 21 of 25 PEP coolers are not 100% full and 2 are below 80%. Utilization fell 5.4 pp to 67.0%.","Coke 13.0% is ahead of Pepsi 10.4%, and MBL’s Cola Next holds 4.8% of facings. 7UP (12.3%) leads Sprite (9.3%)."]},"Faisalabad":{"tag":"Critical","drag":"Availability","why":["Lowest SOS (24.8%) and the only city where KO (28.6%) is ahead of PEP. “Others” is 32.6%.","Availability 13.3%: 26 of 30 stores have no PEP cooler. Of those, 65% have only another brand’s cooler, 23% a KO cooler and 11.5% no cooler.","Only 4 PEP coolers, so Purity 31.3% and Fullness 80.8% are small-base: KO takes 32.7% and other products 30.6% of the space in them.","Coke 14.4% vs Pepsi 5.0% (about 3×); Sprite 13.3% vs 7UP 6.4% (2×)."]},"Gujranwala":{"tag":"Growing, watch purity","drag":"Purity (watch)","why":["SOS 60.4%, up 5.4 pp, but the gain came from stores without a PEP cooler (+5.9 pp), not from the coolers.","Availability 59.4% (+2.2 pp). 13 stores still have no PEP cooler; 85% of them rely on another brand’s cooler.","Purity fell 4.3 pp to 84.5% and Fullness 1.8 pp to 93.5%, so Utilization fell 5.6 pp to 79.0%.","Pepsi (10.8%) is ahead of Coke (9.6%); M.Dew at 10.4% is a strength; 7UP and Sprite are level."]},"Lahore":{"tag":"Critical","drag":"Availability","why":["Largest volume gap: 58 stores, SOS 35.5%, down 6.8 pp, almost entirely from stores without a PEP cooler (−6.3 pp effect).","Availability 34.5%: 38 stores have no PEP cooler, 97% of them with only another brand’s cooler. Other coolers are in 79% of Lahore stores.","“Others” jumped from 25.6% to 41.8% while KO also fell (26.1% to 19.7%): both PEP and KO lost shelf to other products.","Inside PEP coolers KO takes 14.3% of facings (Purity 66.6%) and only 87% of PEP coolers are switched on. Coke 8.4% vs Pepsi 5.5%; Sprite 7.5% vs 7UP 6.1%."]},"Islamabad":{"tag":"Place coolers","drag":"Availability","why":["SOS 72.5% (+15.9 pp) looks strong, but availability is only 18.2%: 9 of 11 stores have no PEP cooler.","Those stores still show 72.5% PEP SOS through other coolers (present in 82% of stores). A PEP cooler would give PEP control of that space.","Only 2 PEP coolers, so Purity −6.0 pp is not reliable.","PEP leads every duel: Pepsi 14.7% vs Coke 9.2%, 7UP 19.8% vs Sprite 7.7%, Mirinda 7.9% vs Fanta 4.3%."]},"Rawalpindi":{"tag":"Strong, place coolers","drag":"Availability (small)","why":["SOS 66.4% (−5.7 pp). Availability 58.3% is flat; the 5 stores without a PEP cooler all rely on another brand’s cooler (KO has none here).","Execution inside coolers is strong: Fullness 97.9%, Purity 90.1%.","SOS is 90.1% in stores with a PEP cooler vs 33.3% in stores without, so cooler placement is the lever.","Pepsi 12.1% vs Coke 5.1%; 7UP 14.7% vs Sprite 4.2%."]},"Peshawar":{"tag":"Benchmark","drag":"None, strongest","why":["Best-run Petro city: Availability 95.2%, Fullness 97.2%, Purity 85.8%, Utilization 83.5%.","SOS 62.6% (+2.7 pp) even though KO has a cooler in 57% of stores.","Pepsi 12.0% vs Coke 8.5%; 7UP 11.9% vs Sprite 7.2%; Sting 12.0% is the highest of any city.","Small gap left: 5 of 20 PEP coolers are not 100% full."]}}}""")

